      "message": "Done in PS3 (PS2 had a checkstyle failure, fixed): plain C and vector literals instead of _mm_*. One part I could not take literally: \u003e\u003e on a vector with a count equal to the element width is undefined (GCC manual: \"undefined if any bi is greater than or equal to B\"), and that is what Clang miscompiles for a constant n \u003d\u003d 2. So the tail is shifted as a scalar and is zero for n equal to the element size. The test fails on the old code and passes on this one with release Clang for default, x86-64-v3 and x86-64-v4.",
